  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2026-02-25T16:02:31.762Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "I moderate for events that do not strictly enforce avatar limits, as our community has expressed they prioritise self expression over performance during events. However, we generally limit the avatar MB above a certain point to discourage users from using exceptionally heavy avatars in large lobbies.\n\nAt present, our team has to manually check the avatar download size of each attendee, as there are no obvious or immediate indicators for this information. In a lobby of 30+ people, this can become time consuming and take away from active moderation of user interactions.\n\nI would be interested in some form of immediate, easily accessible indicator that makes exceptionally large avatar file sizes more obvious.\n\nI am not suggesting an additional performance rank, but instead an indicator that would make this information more immediately readable.\n\nThank you!",
